Ryanair Holdings plc

Description of the incident: On April 30, 2026, new reports emerged confirming that a threat actor had breached Ryanair and leaked sensitive internal flight compensation data, including customer banking details, legal correspondence, and court documents, across underground cybercrime forums ``.

What it means for the company: The exposure of internal legal claims management platforms and procedural notes could compromise active litigation strategies, lead to severe regulatory scrutiny regarding passenger data protection, and significantly damage consumer trust ``.

